  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership for Togo (2026#2030)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government Roadmap 2020-2025, which draws heavily on the National Development Plan 2018-2022, is the strategic and programmatic framework for government priorities up to 2025, and is therefore the current reference source for all development partners in their cooperation frameworks.  UNIDO has a clear comparative advantage through its mandate to support Togo in the implementation process of the Government Roadmap#s second Axis which gives a central role to industrial development. Furthermore, there are great opportunities for UNIDO to expand its portfolio and services in agro- processing and the development of targeted value- chains. A new CP would foster the necessary partner and resource mobilization efforts and tailor the strategic interventions for the country#s inclusive and sustainable industrialization process.  A request letter has been submitted to UNIDO by the government of Togo in January 2024. Moreover, the Togo Minister of Investment in charge of Industrial development recently met with the Director General during the 20th UNIDO General Conference on LDCs in November 2023. The Minister reiterated Togo#s request for the development of a CP. The DG confirmed UNIDO#s will and high interest to develop a CP in the country to upscale TC in Togo, which is underscored in his answer letter to the Minist</narrative>
  </description>
